      "message": "The commit adds a new SCSS class .table-fixed-layout and applies it via table-class\u003d\"table-fixed-layout\" on most tables — but on EventLogs.vue, Dumps.vue, and PostCodeLogs.vue it uses the built-in fixed prop instead. Both do exactly the same thing (table-layout: fixed).\n\nWhy:\nbootstrap-vue-next (v0.40.8, used in this repo) already has a fixed boolean prop on \u003cb-table\u003e. So the new SCSS utility is redundant, and using both mechanisms in the same commit creates two ways to do one thing — future maintainers will not know which to follow. The commit message also claims the class was applied to Event Logs / Dumps / POST Code Logs, but those three actually use the fixed prop.\n\nRecommendation:\nPick one approach and use it everywhere:\n\nPreferred: delete .table-fixed-layout from _tables.scss and use the built-in fixed prop on every touched \u003cb-table\u003e.\nThen update the commit message so it matches the code",
