      "side": 1,
      "message": "In _tables.scss, a new line min-width: 50px; is added inside .table-row-expand.\n\nWhy:\nUnder table-layout: fixed, browsers ignore min-width on \u003ctd\u003e / \u003cth\u003e. Column width is fully controlled by the first row\u0027s \u003cth\u003e width (or the thStyle set in the field definition). Since every touched table now sets an explicit thStyle on the expand column, this new line has zero effect — it\u0027s dead CSS.\n\nRecommendation:\nRemove the min-width: 50px; line. If you want a hard floor for the chevron, put it on the thStyle of the column instead (e.g. thStyle: { width: \u002750px\u0027 })",
