      "side": 1,
      "message": "The chevron/checkbox column is sized inconsistently across the touched files:\n\nEventLogs.vue → thStyle: { width: \u002750px\u0027 }\nDumps.vue / PostCodeLogs.vue → thStyle: { width: \u002748px\u0027 }\nAll InventoryTable*.vue and Sessions.vue → thStyle: { width: \u00274%\u0027 }\nWhy:\nThe chevron button itself is a fixed pixel size. On narrow screens, 4% of the table width can shrink below the button width, causing the chevron to overflow its cell. Also, sibling Inventory sub-tables are supposed to line up on the page — a mix of 4% and 50px breaks that.\n\nRecommendation:\nUse one consistent pixel value (e.g. \u002750px\u0027) for the checkbox / expand-chevron column across every table touched in this change",
